<title>UK: British Steel off after German deal scrapped.</title>
<headline>British Steel off after German deal scrapped.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in British Steel Plc headed lower in a rising market on Tuesday, hit by news that Germany's Krupp Stahl AG was calling off its takeover bid for Thyssen AG, dealers said.</p>
<p>&quot;Consolidation in the European steel industry would have been good for British Steel and it's getting hurt by the failure of the German link-up,&quot; one dealer said.</p>
<p>The shares were down 3-1/4p at 158-1/2 by 0824 GMT.</p>
<p>-- London newsroom +44 171 542 5106</p>
